        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Who makes the rules?"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A new road, a school meal, a vaccination drive: each begins as a decision. Governance is how decisions are made and carried out for a community."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "challenges",
          "contributors",
          "evolution",
          "examples",
          "governance",
          "public policy",
          "stages",
          "why public"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Governance is the way power is used to manage a country's affairs and resources.\nIts meaning has evolved from rule by kings to participation by citizens.\nPublic policy is a plan or action by government to solve a problem for the public.\nIt is called public because it affects everyone and is made with public money and for public benefit.\nPolicy making has stages: identifying the problem, forming the policy, implementing it and evaluating it.\nLegislature, executive, judiciary, experts, media and citizens all contribute.\nPolicies like midday meals and the Right to Education affect daily life.\nChallenges include corruption, delays and lack of awareness; transparency and participation help."
        }
